        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): avoid false unscheduled note after shell cron add",
        "body": "Closes #52972\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users who schedule reminders through a shell-driven `openclaw cron add ...` command could still receive the false note saying no reminder was scheduled in the turn.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe reminder guard already trusts successful structured `cron` tool adds. This extends the same producer-side counter to successful `exec` and `bash` commands that run `openclaw cron add` and return a cron add response shaped like the CLI output. Failed commands and unrelated cron commands are ignored.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers no longer get a contradictory unscheduled-reminder note after a shell cron add succeeds. Failed or unrelated shell commands still leave the guard active.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/embedded-agent-subscribe.handlers.tools.test.ts`\n  - `Test Files  1 passed (1)`\n  - `Tests  83 passed (83)`\n- `pnpm exec oxfmt --check --threads=1 src/agents/embedded-agent-subscribe.handlers.tools.ts src/agents/embedded-agent-subscribe.handlers.tools.test.ts`\n  - `All matched files use the correct format.`\n- `pnpm changed:lanes --json`\n  - `lanes: core, coreTests`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `pnpm check:changed`\n  - Remote Testbox delegation failed locally because Crabbox failed its binary sanity check before repo checks ran.\n  - Reran the delegated child command locally: `env OPENCLAW_CHECK_CHANGED_REMOTE_CHILD=1 OPENCLAW_CHANGED_LANES_RAW_SYNC=1 CI=1 PNPM_CONFIG_VERIFY_DEPS_BEFORE_RUN=false corepack pnpm check:changed`, which passed.",
